{"rev":7,"ts":"2026-10-24T02:16:56.275502376+00:00","fields":{"__previous_part_content__":"1. After approval, register distinct `mission-cli` and `mission-mcp` artifacts in the canonical installer registry.\n2. Verify registry selection/catalog behavior and both installed help commands.\n3. Verify a direct-authoring fixture using installed artifacts and explicit workspace selection, including stored Mission ID/revision read-back.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Registry/catalog validation reports both IDs with no duplicate or missing entry.\n- install-ctl recognizes both selected IDs.\n- Installed `mission --help` and `mission-mcp --help` succeed.\n- Missing entry, failed help, or failed direct-authoring read-back blocks pilot publication.\n","__previous_part_id__":"624837ab-15d3-4ea3-ab62-5bf297a37f1a","component":"mission.installer-distribution","depends_on":["57161cbd-58fc-44a3-9528-baa4cd1fceac"],"effort":"1k","parts":[{"id":"624837ab-15d3-4ea3-ab62-5bf297a37f1a","kind":"requirements","path":"parts/requirements.md","frozen":false,"created_at":"2026-10-24T02:06:54.076852105Z"}],"priority":"high","related_specs":"38a8ea3a-9a6a-4a0f-bc5a-97dc9ba670fc,9e714b78-ef31-46e5-8103-a944e7b1a278","state":"planning","title":"[mission][install-ctl] Register Mission CLI and MCP artifacts","type":"task"}}
{"rev":8,"ts":"2026-10-24T02:17:07.373831325+00:00","fields":{"__previous_part_content__":"1. After approval, register distinct `mission-cli` and `mission-mcp` artifacts in the canonical installer registry; retain unrelated installer work, including `install/install.sh`.\n2. Verify registry selection/catalog behavior and exact scoped installation: `install-ctl install --root <ROOT> <SELECTION>...`; for this pilot use root `/home/linus/.copilot/session-state/ae41c0ca-75fa-497e-b4ac-90e3fa04f6ec/files/mission-install-pilot-install` and selections `mission-cli mission-mcp`.\n3. Verify installed `mission --help`. Verify installed `mission-mcp` only through stdio JSON-RPC in isolated workspace cwd `/home/linus/.copilot/session-state/ae41c0ca-75fa-497e-b4ac-90e3fa04f6ec/files/mission-install-pilot-workspace`: `initialize` → `notifications/initialized` → `tools/list` → `tools/call`, followed by process cleanup; never use `mission-mcp --help`.\n4. Installed direct operations must create, validate, publish, and get by the real stored ID/current revision, with persisted content and typed result evidence read-back and no external manifest/dossier input.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Registry/catalog validation reports exactly both IDs with no duplicate or missing entry; `catalog --check` passes.\n- `install-ctl` recognizes both selected IDs and exact scoped installation yields both binaries under the isolated root.\n- Installed CLI help succeeds; MCP protocol flow returns structured success/error assertions and cleanup evidence.\n- Installed direct-operation fixture reads back actual ID, revision, content, validation/publication state, and result evidence; any failure blocks pilot publication.\n- W2 evidence runs `cargo test -p install-ctl --test install_parity --test prebuilt_install`, catalog check, and the exact scoped install.\n","__previous_part_id__":"624837ab-15d3-4ea3-ab62-5bf297a37f1a","component":"mission.installer-distribution","depends_on":["57161cbd-58fc-44a3-9528-baa4cd1fceac"],"effort":"1k","parts":[{"id":"624837ab-15d3-4ea3-ab62-5bf297a37f1a","kind":"requirements","path":"parts/requirements.md","frozen":false,"created_at":"2026-10-24T02:06:54.076852105Z"}],"priority":"high","related_specs":"38a8ea3a-9a6a-4a0f-bc5a-97dc9ba670fc,9e714b78-ef31-46e5-8103-a944e7b1a278","state":"planning","title":"[mission][install-ctl] Register Mission CLI and MCP artifacts","type":"task"}}
